EmberBSD local, AI-assisted; not submitted upstream.
Cross-build support for the GCC test-suite harness on macOS targeting
EmberBSD/AArch64. Applies on top of the development-toolchain export
(pkgsrc fff4deb639a1a640476203c80f752fb77b6cb14b plus stable-expect).

- lang/tcl: neutralize the raw build-host uname gates (Darwin APIs,
  -dynamiclib, wide clicks) and override the uname-derived system
  version with EMBER_CROSS_TARGET_SYS for the bundled package
  configures; tclConfig.sh keeps target-only paths.
- lang/tcl-expect: nine runtime probes refuse cross builds; each
  decision now reads a NetBSD/11 aarch64 answer taken from native
  probes in the reference VM on 2026-10-14 (WNOHANG present,
  sgttyb/termios structs, TIOCGWINSZ, timezone variable; no termio,
  no Cray ptys, no TCGETS/TCGETA). NetBSD setpgrp(pid, pgid) takes two
  arguments. K&R prototypes need -std=gnu89 with GCC16. The install
  step regenerates wrapper scripts with the host tclsh. Darwin linker
  flags and tcl private headers resolve like lang/tcl.
- devel/dejagnu: the cross build cannot run the target install-info;
  the info index is registered on the target after installation.

The packages were accepted in the AArch64 VM: tcl-8.6.18,
tcl-expect-5.45.4nb1, dejagnu-1.6.3 (see the E8 receipt in the wiki).

